      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/12/beau-lamarre-condon-jesse-baird-phone-murder-trial-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Court hears former police officer agrees he was trying to destroy evidence that might incriminate him</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Beau Lamarre-Condon has admitted he threw Jesse Baird’s phone off a bridge to destroy evidence after allegedly murdering him, a court has heard.</p><p>The former police officer is accused of fatally shooting Baird and his new partner, Luke Davies, with his police service weapon in Baird’s Paddington home in Sydney on 19 February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/12/beau-lamarre-condon-jesse-baird-phone-murder-trial-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
