      "title": "Australian states could sue tobacco companies for billions in healthcare costs under proposal",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/12/australian-states-could-sue-tobacco-companies-for-billions-smoking-healthcare-costs",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive: </strong>Former barrister who helped legally establish that secondhand smoke causes lung cancer argues states could seek up to $50bn in compensation</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australian state governments could sue tobacco companies for billions in public hospital and healthcare costs, under a proposal developed by a former barrister who helped legally establish that secondhand smoke causes lung cancer.</p><p>The South Australian government is formally seeking advice on the proposal, while other states are reviewing it.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/12/australian-states-could-sue-tobacco-companies-for-billions-smoking-healthcare-costs\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-12T01:02:01"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hacker claims to have sold VCE exam papers to hundreds of students after government website hack",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/12/vce-exams-hack-year-12-papers-vcaa-victorian-curriculum-and-assessment-authority",
      "description": "<p>With year 12 exams under way, VCAA says there is no evidence any have leaked and hacker is attempting to exploit ‘anxious students’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Victorian Curriculum and Assessment Authority’s website has been hacked during the state’s exam period, with the culprit launching a tirade of expletives and claiming without evidence to have accessed student papers.</p><p>On Wednesday evening, a message attributed to someone using the alias “DaggerElite” appeared on the VCAA’s homepage banner, claiming to have sold exam papers to “hundreds of students” across the state.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/12/vce-exams-hack-year-12-papers-vcaa-victorian-curriculum-and-assessment-authority\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-11T23:28:17"
    },
